  "query_preview": "(Today through Saturday)...\nIssued at 251 AM EDT Sun Aug 2 2026\n\nSurface analysis early this morning shows low pressure centered over \nCentral Indiana.  Radar shows a few showers across the northwest \nparts of the forecast area, stretching from Tipton to near Terre \nHaute, spinning around the low. GOES shows abundant cloud cover in \nplace across the forecast area due to the low. Water vapor imagery \nshows a deep trough in place over Indiana with strong ridging over \nthe northern plains. Subsidence was filling into the low from the \nsouthwest, wrapping across KY and into SW OH.\n\nToday...\n\nModels continue to keep the upper low lingering across Indiana, \nslowly sagging southeast. The associated surface low will push \nacross Indiana today before reaching Appalachia tonight. Time \nheights through the day keep plentiful lower level moisture \navailable and this should lead to continued periodic light showers. \nHeavier rain is not expected as dry air continues to infiltrate the \nsystem. Thus will continue to use high pops today for light \nprecipitation amounts. Clouds and precip will keep temperatures down, \nresulting in below normal highs in the middle 70s.\n\nTonight...stronger surface high pressure is suggested to build \nacross WI and MI and spill into Indiana. This will result in \ncontinued clearing skies as the earlier low drifts east and mid \nlevel dry air and subsidence arrives across Indiana. Thus clearing \nskies this evening. Lows will only fall to the middle 60s.\n\nMonday and Tuesday...\n\nStrong mid level ridging in place over the upper midwest on Monday \nand Tuesday will continue to provide strong subsidence and dry air \nacross Indiana to start the work week. Forecast soundings show a \nvery dry column in place with a mid level inversion in place each \nafternoon. Meanwhile strong surface high pressure will be moving \nacross the southern Great Lakes, providing cooler easterly flow. \nThus expect mostly sunny days and mostly clear nights with high sin \nthe middle 80s.\n\nWednesday...\n\nDry weather appears in store on Wednesday as high pressure \nstretching from the upper midwest and across the Great Lakes will \ncontinue to maintain control of our weather. Forecast soundings \nsuggest a dry column on Wednesday that should lead to just partly \ncloudy skies.\n\nThursday through Saturday...\n\nThe upper pattern during this period looks to consist of shallow and \nbroad troughing in place across the northern CONUS east of the \nRockies. A few embedded short waves look to pass during this time \nwithin the flow aloft. Within the lower levels a weak frontal \nboundary is depicted lingering across Indiana on Thursday into \nFriday. This lower level convergence in combination with weak \nforcing aloft and more humid air mass in place will result in the \nneed for pops each day. By Saturday, warm and humid southerly flow \nis depicted. Forecast soundings show steep lapse rates favorable for \ndiurnal convection. Thus once again, pops will need to be included \non Saturday.",
